/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   ONE THREAD, ONE HEADER (18 Nov 2026). A request's or a change's page is
   drawn on its own page, in the Workshop's panel beside the list and in the
   column beside Homeroom bot's list. Each surface used to wrap it in chrome
   of its own: a "‹ Workshop" chip over the page, a sheet with a bar of ×
   and "Open as a page" around the Workshop's panel, a second header row and
   a white column around the bot's. Now every surface draws the same thing:

     - the sheet's bar is the thread's HEAD (a pill until 19 Nov 2026, a
       card since): the project's tile, a small line with the project, the
       topic, "Change #N" or "Request #N" and its status pill, the title,
       ⋯, and in a panel ↗ and × (dev-board/topic/thread-exits.tsx). On
       the page itself the page's way back sits at the head's start.
     - it FLOATS over the top of the thread and stays there: the scroller
       starts under it, so the cards go up behind it as the reader scrolls.
     - the cards below it lie on the page's own ground. No panel draws a
       sheet, a border or a second header around them.

   The card's kicker said the project, the number and the topic; the head
   says them now, and the title, so the card starts at its words.

   Only the standard and the brand looks (the thread card's own pages); the
   frame's looks keep their kit's head. `!important` is spent only where a
   rule above names the page's whole ancestry to place the old bar.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
html:is(:not([data-skin]), [data-skin="brand"]) .dev-request:has(.dev-thread-card) {
  /* The head's height, read off the head itself (thread-head-fit.ts): one
     line of title or two, at whatever width the page is. */
  --pill-h: var(--thread-head-h, 104px);
  --pill-top: 8px;
  --pill-under: calc(var(--pill-top) + var(--pill-h) + 12px);
  /* The middle of the head's tile, from its top: where the way back sits. */
  --head-mid: 38px;
  position: relative;
}
html:is(:not([data-skin]), [data-skin="brand"]) .dev-request[data-thread-head-tight]:has(.dev-thread-card) { --head-mid: 28px; }
/* In a panel the head starts on the column's own top line, level with the
   first card of the list beside it (Homeroom bot's own head card, the
   Workshop's list). */
html:is(:not([data-skin]), [data-skin="brand"]) :is(.dev-ws-side, .in-side-panel body) .dev-request:has(.dev-thread-card),
html:is(:not([data-skin]), [data-skin="brand"]) #ai-screen .dev-private-thread:has(.dev-thread-card) { --pill-top: 0px; }
html:is(:not([data-skin]), [data-skin="brand"]) .dev-request:has(.dev-thread-card) > .dev-request-sheet { position: relative; }
html:is(:not([data-skin]), [data-skin="brand"]) :is(#dev-topic-thread, #ai-screen) .dev-request:has(.dev-thread-card) .dev-request-bar {
  display: block !important;
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  inset-inline: 0;
  z-index: 6;
  height: auto;
  padding-block: var(--pill-top) 0;
  box-shadow: none;
  animation: none;
  pointer-events: none;
}
/* THE THREAD'S HEAD IS A CARD (19 Nov 2026). It was a 56px capsule with a
   drop shadow, the only rounded-end shape on a page of 20px cards, and it
   named the thread by its number while the card under it said the title.
   It is now the column's own card: the cards' corners and edge, the
   project's tile, a small line (the project, the topic, "Request #N" and
   where it stands) over the TITLE, in two lines at most; the card under it
   starts at the request's own words. Only ⋯ keeps a disc; in a panel ↗ and
   × follow it as plain icons, after a thin line. Scrolled, the head
   tightens to one line of title over the small line
   (`data-thread-head-tight`, thread-head-fit.ts), and the cards go up
