/* ── THE BRAND LOOK: PAPER, SIMPLIFIED, WITH BRAND STYLING (Settings ›
   Experimental › Look, an admin's preview) ──
   Every rule here is scoped to html[data-skin="brand"], which the head's
   window.Skin sets from the device's stored choice before this sheet
   applies; without it not one rule below matches. It is drawn in light
   and in dark, where the shell and a framed app agree about the tone:
   light is :not(.dark):not([data-app-tone="dark"]), dark is
   .dark:not([data-app-tone="light"]), as the frame's looks scope their
   pages. Where the two disagree (a dark app under the light shell, a
   light app under the dark one) the look steps aside and the standard
   rules draw the page.

   WRITTEN ONCE FOR BOTH MODES. Each mode sets the look's own colours as
   --bl-* variables on <html>, beside the product's tokens, and the rules
   below read them from a scope that matches either mode. Only the two
   ramps that repaint Tailwind's zinc and violet utilities are per mode:
   light and dark wear different utility classes (bg-zinc-100 and
   dark:bg-zinc-800), so each mode names its own.

   The id is the old New look's ("Baseplate", request #6278), whose switch
   is gone. This is that look redrawn (13 Nov 2026): the Paper look's manner
   on the STANDARD pages, in the website's colours and typefaces.
   - Same pages. It is not a look of the frame: no page changes its markup
     or its layout, so every rule here is paint.
   - Figure and ground. The page is one deeper cream and a card is plain
     white with a soft lift and no outline, so a card differs from the page
     by its fill. (The website's own cream, #fffeea, is too close to white
     for that without the ink outline its cards wear.) In dark the page is
     a very dark navy, a card is one step lighter in the same blue, and
     words are a white tinted the same way.
   - A frame around the page: a deep sky sidebar with white words, and a
     navy top bar, darker than the sidebar so the two read as two pieces. A
     community's own header colour stays on its pages. In dark both are
     much deeper, a dark blue sidebar under a navy bar, so the frame does
     not glare beside a dark page.
   - One job per colour. Sun (#ffee6f) means "you are here" on the sidebar
     and the tab bar, and "do this" on the main button, which in light also
     wears the website's ink outline and hard foot. In dark the sun is
     turned down a step (#f3d920) and the button is flat. Deep sky (#1a63c4) is a
     link, and a count that asks for you; in dark a link is a light sky,
     which reads on a dark card. Ink (#121a0e) is text; in dark, text is
     a white tinted toward the page's blue.
   - Two families, in both modes. Light is yellow (the cream page, sun)
     and blue (the frame, links). Dark is the same two with the roles
     turned: blue is the page and everything on it, and sun is the accent.
   - Geist for words and for titles, Geist Mono for counts. A label over
     a group is sentence case, not small caps.
   - The website's own figures in two empty states.

   Appended last on purpose. The declarations other rules count (the home
   washes, the wallpaper, the sheet fill) are not redeclared: the ground,
   the bars and the planes are painted over them instead. */
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Geist';
  /* Absolute: the build-scoped copy of this sheet (/b/<sha>/css/app.css)
     serves only .js and .css, so a relative url would 404 there. A browser
     without this look never matches a rule that names Geist, so it never
     downloads the file. The same holds for the two faces below. */
  src: url('/fonts/geist/Geist-Variable.woff2') format('woff2');
  font-weight: 100 900;
  font-style: normal;
  font-display: swap;
}
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Geist Mono';
  src: url('/fonts/geist-mono/GeistMono-Variable.woff2') format('woff2');
  font-weight: 100 900;
  font-style: normal;
  font-display: swap;
}
/* No rule of this look names Young Serif since its titles went back to
   Geist. The face stays declared, and its file committed, for the
   signed-out pages' look, which draws its headlines in it. */
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Source Serif 4';
  src: url('/fonts/source-serif-4/source-serif-4-latin-opsz-normal.woff2') format('woff2');
  font-weight: 200 900;
  font-style: normal;
  font-display: swap;
}
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Young Serif';
  src: url('/fonts/young-serif/young-serif-latin-400-normal.woff2') format('woff2');
  font-weight: 400;
  font-style: normal;
  font-display: swap;
}
html[data-skin="brand"]:is(:not(.dark):not([data-app-tone="dark"]), .dark:not([data-app-tone="light"])) {
  font-family: 'Geist', ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif, "Apple Color Emoji", "Segoe UI Emoji", "Segoe UI Symbol", "Noto Color Emoji";
  background-color: var(--bl-page);
}
/* LIGHT. */
html[data-skin="brand"]:not(.dark):not([data-app-tone="dark"]) {
  /* The look's own colours, read by the rules below. */
  --bl-page: #f6f2d8;
  --bl-card: #ffffff;
  --bl-raise: #ffffff;
  --bl-label: #41483c;
  --bl-tile-ink: #595f52;
  --bl-bar: #37477b;
  /* The sidebar fades from --bl-side at its top to --bl-side-end at its
     foot: a step lighter and softer than the deep sky (#1a63c4) it was, so
     it sits back from the content (Drea's review of #6699). */
  --bl-side: #3c7bd8;
  --bl-side-end: #3370d0;
  /* The page's washes, as r, g, b: the standard wallpaper's lilac, pink and
     peach moved round the cream, to a lighter cream, a blush and a sun. */
  --bl-wash-a: 255, 253, 240;
  --bl-wash-b: 247, 220, 200;
  --bl-wash-c: 251, 230, 175;
  /* The splotches the light page wears in their place (THE SPLOTCHES,
     below): the standard wallpaper's own lilac, pink and peach, as r, g, b,
     scattered thin over the cream. Light only: dark keeps its washes. */
  --bl-splotch-a: 229, 216, 239;
  --bl-splotch-b: 245, 215, 230;
  --bl-splotch-c: 252, 219, 212;
  /* Home's cards lift a little further off the washes. */
  --bl-lift-home: 0 1px 2px rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.05), 0 18px 40px -22px rgba(70, 50, 20, 0.38);
  --bl-sun: #ffee6f;
  --bl-sun-lit: #fff6ac;
  --bl-on-sun: #121a0e;
  --bl-wash: #fff6ac;
  --bl-sky: #1a63c4;
  --bl-count: #1a63c4;
  --bl-on-count: #ffffff;
  --bl-solid: #121a0e;
  --bl-on-solid: #ffffff;
  --bl-tint-sun: #fff6ac;
  --bl-tint-sky: #e3eefb;
  /* The row open beside the board: a breath of warmth, and its edge. */
  --bl-row-on: #f9f7ea;
  --bl-row-on-edge: rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.28);
  /* The line round a message's bubble, and round your own on sky. */
  --bl-bubble-line: rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.14);
  --bl-bubble-line-own: rgba(26, 99, 196, 0.24);
  --bl-card-line: rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.2);
  --bl-tint-leaf: #e2f2dc;
  --bl-on-tint: #121a0e;
  --bl-edge: rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.07);
  --bl-pic-line: rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.1);
  --bl-lift: 0 1px 2px rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.06), 0 14px 30px -22px rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.3);
  --bl-raise-edge: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.1), 0 1px 2px rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.06);
  /* A field on a card (a reply box): firmer than a raised button's edge. */
  --bl-field-edge: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.16), 0 1px 2px rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.06);
  --bl-pill-edge: inset 0 0 0 1px #121a0e, 0 2px 0 #121a0e;
  --bl-pill-edge-down: inset 0 0 0 1px #121a0e, 0 0 0 #121a0e;
  /* Surfaces: white cards on the cream page. */
  --bg-primary: #ffffff;
  --bg-secondary: #f6f2d8;
  --bg-tertiary: #ece8cc;
  --bg-input: #ffffff;
  --dc-strip: #f6f2d8;
  --dc-sheet: #ffffff;
  --dc-sheet-raise: #ffffff;
  --dc-raised: #f6f2d8;
  --dc-sheet-solid: #ffffff;
  --dc-strip-solid: #f6f2d8;
  --border: rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.14);
  --border-light: rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.08);
  /* Ink and its warm greys. */
  --text-primary: #121a0e;
  --text-secondary: #41483c;
  --text-muted: #595f52;
  --text-faint: #858a7c;
  /* The old blue's jobs that are not a link or a count go to ink: text,
     outlines, a switch that is on and the quieter fills. Sun and the deep
     sky are given out by name below. */
  --accent: #121a0e;
  --accent-light: #41483c;
  --accent-ink: #ffffff;
  --accent-tint: rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.06);
  --accent-tint-ink: #121a0e;
  --accent-wash: #fff6ac;
  --accent-wash-ink: #121a0e;
  /* Lit things on the page (steps, tags, the theme switch) on a pale sun.
     The sidebar and the bars set their own below. */
  --lit-ink: #121a0e;
  --lit-tint: #fff6ac;
  --lit-line: transparent;
  /* The header's ink where it is read off the bar (a place bar, a sheet's
     head). Both bars set white on themselves below. */
  --brand-ink: #121a0e;
  --brand-tint: #ffffff;
  --brand-line: rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.1);
}
/* Hairlines in ink at 7%, unless high contrast asked for darker ones. A
   card's own outline is this faint too: its fill and lift say where it
   ends. */
html[data-skin="brand"]:not(.dark):not([data-app-tone="dark"]):not([data-contrast="more"]) {
  --app-sheet-line: rgba(18, 26, 14, 0.07);
}
/* DARK. The same roles on a very dark navy page, so dark is the look's
   own blue and yellow and nothing else. It was first a deep green (the
   dark of the website's ink), then a dark purple after the standard
   dark's washes: each was a third family beside the blue frame and the
   sun accents, and purple fought the sun, its opposite. As in the standard
   dark the surfaces climb from the page: --bg-primary is the page, a card
   is --bg-secondary, and what stands on a card is --bg-tertiary. The greys
   are tinted toward the same blue. */
html[data-skin="brand"].dark:not([data-app-tone="light"]) {
  --bl-page: #0d1421;
  --bl-card: #182135;
  --bl-raise: #243047;
  --bl-label: #c3cad8;
  --bl-tile-ink: #c3cad8;
  --bl-bar: #232b43;
  --bl-side: #122a52;
  --bl-side-end: #122a52;
  /* The washes round the navy, all blues as the dark look is: a lighter
     navy, a deeper blue and a deep sky. */
  --bl-wash-a: 30, 42, 68;
  --bl-wash-b: 24, 38, 84;
  --bl-wash-c: 22, 50, 82;
  /* Dark keeps the washes (THE SPLOTCHES are light's), so its splotch
     colours are the washes' own blues, set only so each mode has the
     look's every colour. */
  --bl-splotch-a: 30, 42, 68;
  --bl-splotch-b: 24, 38, 84;
  --bl-splotch-c: 22, 50, 82;
  --bl-lift-home: var(--bl-lift);
  /* The sun turned down, not washed out (19 Nov 2026): the light's full
     sun (#ffee6f, oklch .94 .148 102) glared as a fill on the navy, and a
     darker one went olive because it lost its colour too. This is a step
     dimmer at the most colour the screen can show for it (oklch .88 .18
     100), so it reads as the same lit yellow with the light turned down. */
  --bl-sun: #f3d920;
  --bl-sun-lit: #f8e24c;
  --bl-on-sun: #121a0e;
  --bl-wash: rgba(255, 238, 111, 0.14);
  --bl-sky: #7fbcf7;
  --bl-count: #1a63c4;
  --bl-on-count: #ffffff;
  --bl-solid: #eef2f8;
  --bl-on-solid: #0d1421;
  --bl-tint-sun: rgba(255, 238, 111, 0.18);
  --bl-tint-sky: rgba(127, 188, 247, 0.18);
  --bl-row-on: rgba(220, 230, 248, 0.04);
  --bl-row-on-edge: rgba(220, 230, 248, 0.38);
  --bl-bubble-line: rgba(220, 230, 248, 0.2);
  --bl-bubble-line-own: rgba(127, 188, 247, 0.42);
  --bl-card-line: rgba(220, 230, 248, 0.26);
  --bl-tint-leaf: rgba(150, 184, 133, 0.22);
  --bl-on-tint: #eef2f8;
  --bl-edge: rgba(220, 230, 248, 0.08);
  --bl-pic-line: rgba(220, 230, 248, 0.12);
  /* A shadow has to out-darken the page to lift anything from it. */
  --bl-lift: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35), 0 14px 30px -22px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.9);
  --bl-raise-edge: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(220, 230, 248, 0.1), 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
  --bl-field-edge: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(220, 230, 248, 0.14), 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  /* An ink outline would vanish on the dark page, and the hard foot in a
     deeper sun it had instead read as yellow on gold: the pill is flat. */
  --bl-pill-edge: 0 0 0 transparent;
  --bl-pill-edge-down: 0 0 0 transparent;
  --bg-primary: #0d1421;
  --bg-secondary: #182135;
  --bg-tertiary: #243047;
  --dev-press: #303e5a;
  --bg-input: #182135;
  --bg-code: #0a0f1a;
  --bg-code-header: #182135;
  --bg-card: rgba(220, 230, 248, 0.06);
  --dc-strip: #0d1421;
  --dc-sheet: #182135;
  --dc-sheet-raise: #243047;
  --dc-raised: #243047;
  --dc-sheet-solid: #182135;
  --dc-strip-solid: #0d1421;
  /* In dark the lighter line is the stronger one, as in the standard dark. */
  --border: rgba(220, 230, 248, 0.12);
  --border-light: rgba(220, 230, 248, 0.18);
  /* White and its greys, tinted toward the page. */
  --text-primary: #eef2f8;
  --text-secondary: #d5dbe6;
  --text-muted: #a0a9bb;
  --text-faint: #838da1;
  --text-code: #d5dbe6;
  /* The accent is the light sky here, not the white that would mirror
     light's ink: rules that put white words on the accent stay as readable
     as they are in the standard dark. */
  --accent: #7fbcf7;
  --accent-light: #a9d2fa;
  --accent-ink: #121a0e;
  --accent-tint: rgba(127, 188, 247, 0.14);
  --accent-tint-ink: #7fbcf7;
  --accent-wash: rgba(255, 238, 111, 0.14);
  --accent-wash-ink: #ffee6f;
  /* Lit things on the page: sun words on a wash of sun. */
  --lit-ink: #ffee6f;
  --lit-tint: rgba(255, 238, 111, 0.16);
  --lit-line: transparent;
  --brand-ink: #eef2f8;
  --brand-tint: #182135;
  --brand-line: rgba(220, 230, 248, 0.14);
}
/* Hairlines in that white at 7%, unless high contrast asked for stronger ones. */
html[data-skin="brand"].dark:not([data-app-tone="light"]):not([data-contrast="more"]) {
  --app-sheet-line: rgba(220, 230, 248, 0.07);
}

/* THE PAGE. The wallpaper is drawn on <body> by the route rule (one id
   deep); `:has(#platform-tabs)` is always true in the shell and makes this
   rule one id deep as well, so it wins by its classes. The tile zoom paints
   the moving view from --un-zoom-bg, so it follows. --home-ground moves with
   it: the browser scroller paints the body from it (!important), and the
   launch cover and the washes end on it. The scroller's fixed layer repaints
   the wallpaper.

   THE WASHES (Drea's review of #6699). The page is the standard wallpaper
   again, its washes at exactly the places, sizes and strengths the standard
   look draws them, but in the look's own tints round the cream (--bl-wash-*
   above; round the navy in dark), so the page stays the brand's cream with
   soft light moving across it. Its grain and halftone star come with it, the
   star below the navy bar rather than under it; from 640px two more copies
   of the star, larger and quieter, sit lower on the page. The star and the
   grain are the route rule's variables, so each falls back to nothing on a
   screen that rule does not name rather than voiding the whole background.
   In light the washes give way to THE SPLOTCHES (below); dark keeps them. */
html[data-skin="brand"]:is(:not(.dark):not([data-app-tone="dark"]), .dark:not([data-app-tone="light"])) body:has(#platform-tabs) {
  --home-ground: var(--bl-page);
  --un-zoom-bg: var(--bl-page);
  --look-washes:
    radial-gradient(circle at calc(100% - 92px) 115px, rgba(var(--bl-wash-a), 0.55) 138px, rgba(var(--bl-wash-a), 0.275) 198px, rgba(var(--bl-wash-a), 0) 258px) 0 0 / 100% 100% no-repeat,
    radial-gradient(circle at calc(100% - 62px) 59%, rgba(var(--bl-wash-b), 0.65) 50px, rgba(var(--bl-wash-b), 0.325) 120px, rgba(var(--bl-wash-b), 0) 190px) 0 0 / 100% 100% no-repeat,
    radial-gradient(circle at 70px calc(100% - 69px), rgba(var(--bl-wash-c), 0.75) 90px, rgba(var(--bl-wash-c), 0.375) 170px, rgba(var(--bl-wash-c), 0) 250px) 0 0 / 100% 100% no-repeat var(--bl-page);
  --look-stars: var(--home-star, none) right 40px top calc(var(--home-star-y, 0px) + 64px) / 120px 97px no-repeat;
  --look-wallpaper: var(--look-stars), var(--home-grain, none) 0 0 / 240px 240px repeat, var(--look-washes);
  background: var(--look-wallpaper);
}
@media (min-width: 640px) {
  html[data-skin="brand"]:is(:not(.dark):not([data-app-tone="dark"]), .dark:not([data-app-tone="light"])) body:has(#platform-tabs) {
    --look-washes:
      radial-gradient(circle at calc(100% - 92px) 115px, rgba(var(--bl-wash-a), 0.55) 138px, rgba(var(--bl-wash-a), 0.275) 198px, rgba(var(--bl-wash-a), 0) 258px) 0 0 / 100% 100% no-repeat,
      radial-gradient(circle at calc(100% - 62px) 59%, rgba(var(--bl-wash-b), 0.65) 50px, rgba(var(--bl-wash-b), 0.325) 120px, rgba(var(--bl-wash-b), 0) 190px) 0 0 / 100% 100% no-repeat,
      radial-gradient(circle at 70px calc(100% - 69px), rgba(var(--bl-wash-c), 0.75) 90px, rgba(var(--bl-wash-c), 0.375) 170px, rgba(var(--bl-wash-c), 0) 250px) 0 0 / 100% 100% no-repeat,
      radial-gradient(ellipse 38vw 36vh at 24% 20%, rgba(var(--bl-wash-a), 0.65), rgba(var(--bl-wash-a), 0) 70%) 0 0 / 100% 100% no-repeat,
      radial-gradient(ellipse 36vw 32vh at 66% 76%, rgba(var(--bl-wash-b), 0.65), rgba(var(--bl-wash-b), 0) 70%) 0 0 / 100% 100% no-repeat,
      radial-gradient(ellipse 32vw 32vh at 4% 64%, rgba(var(--bl-wash-c), 0.7), rgba(var(--bl-wash-c), 0) 70%) 0 0 / 100% 100% no-repeat,
